// `holds:` declares C integers a handle holds for its `release:`: each a C declaration of an integer
// the release uses, never `self` or the `kept:` name, on a class neither `shared` nor with `retain:`.
// error: `holds:` declares a C integer, such as a descriptor, and `double` is not one
// error: `holds:` declares `sock` for `release:` to use, and it does not
// error: `self` is the handle's own pointer, so what `holds:` declares has another name
// error: a `shared` handle may be used by any thread, and what it `holds:` is set by the handle's owner alone; a class with `holds:` is not `shared`
// error: a class with `retain:` gives back one C reference of many, and what it `holds:` is the one handle's, given back with its last; a class with `holds:` declares no `retain:`

@c(type: "struct conn *", holds: "double sock", release: "conn_free(self, sock)")
class NotInteger

@c(type: "struct conn *", holds: "int sock = -1", release: "conn_free(self)")
class Unused

@c(type: "struct conn *", holds: "int self", release: "conn_free(self)")
class Self

@c(type: "struct conn *", holds: "int sock", release: "conn_free(self, sock)", shared)
class Shared

@c(type: "struct conn *", holds: "int sock", release: "conn_free(self, sock)", retain: "conn_ref")
class Counted

main() = 0
